        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The Toronto Maple Leafs aren't just reshuffling a roster; they're purging a front office. <strong>Assistant General Manager Hayley Wickenheiser and Associate General Manager Mark Leach have been relieved of their duties in a sweeping front-office purge</strong>, signaling a hard reset after a season that ended in disappointment with just 78 points and an 8th-place finish in the Atlantic Division. The move, which also includes Dave Morrison, underscores a team desperate to rebuild its identity from the inside out, not just on the ice. With Nick Paul's role still being fine-tuned - his ideal linemates remain a key offseason puzzle - the Leafs must now decide whether to gamble on draft picks or chase free agents to fill the gaps. <strong>What to watch: whether the new leadership prioritizes aggressive free-agent signings or a long-term draft strategy to rebuild the core</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated July 10, 2026"
      },
